For some time now I've used some shell script utility to display the
learned spells and their respective expiry time in a somewhat easier
to recognize timely sorted order; then it's easier to recognize which
spellbooks to carry along and which ones to leave behind in the stash.
I found that utility to be helpful accompanying my games so I rewrote
it for web access to maybe be of use for other folks as well...

http://nethack.gridbug.de/spell_expiry.html

It requires some spell naming management, though; after a spell is
successfully learned I immediately give that spellbook class the
_current time_ as name[*], e.g. T:12345. This name won't be displayed
in the inventory list because the spell is already known then, but it
will be visible in the list of discoveries.[**]

Copy/paste the spellbooks section of the discovery list to the left
textarea of the above page, enter the current time, and hit the sort
button.

Janis

[*] Name it, but *not* the "individual" object.

[**] For example as
   spellbook of confuse monster called T:37657 (green)
   spellbook of detect treasure called T:23547 (magenta)


